module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_witness_red_survives_on_main_because_no_gate_runs_its_entry

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data a_witness_red_survives_on_main_because_no_gate_runs_its_entry: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_witness_red_survives_on_main_because_no_gate_runs_its_entry" as NonEmptyStr,
  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a committed witness is red against main itself -- running its entry through claim_batch claim-run on origin/main's own tree fails the claim -- and no gate ever sees it: the required floor selects witnesses by the edited test fns of an integration head's diff, and a main push runs no head diff, so an entry nobody is currently editing is never executed anywhere. The red is silent until an unrelated PR happens to touch the entry, at which point main's defect lands on the PR as if it were the PR's regression.",

    "HARM: main's witness corpus asserts green that is false. The defective witness keeps ratifying nothing on main; the author of the next PR touching the entry either blocks on a red they did not cause, or repairs it out of scope in a PR whose review was calibrated for a different change -- both cost a review cycle and neither was main's price to pay.",

    "SPECIMEN (measured 2026-10-07 by vivid-lynx-377, remote runner, claim_batch claim-run against a checkout of origin/main itself): dag/test/claim/self_host_emitted_call_target_realization_witness_test.dag witness w_depth_one_shared_field_refutation_stays_shape_guarded FAILs on main (exit=1, FAIL=1). The witness synthesizes a std-types-only probe (a shared coproduct matched at depth one inside a record pattern) and imports neither v2.std.optional nor any renamed spelling; the red predates every edit on the discovering branch, where the same entry otherwise runs 59/60. The three sibling reds in the same entry were defunct v2.std.optional probe imports from the #13388 re-homing -- also never exercised on main -- and were repaired on the discovering PR.",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS: the witness fails with no PR diff touching its entry; the failure is in the probe's own compile (compile.frontend), not in an assertion about a consumer; an entry-scoped full-corpus run reproduces it on main and only on main. A witness that is red for a reason the discovering PR's changes could plausibly cause is NOT this row -- attribute first by running the entry on main's own tree.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable. The failure is real but out-of-band: today the only reproducers are a full-corpus run or the next unlucky PR. CEILING: structurally guaranteed -- main's own CI can run the full witness corpus the way a PR's floor does, with no diff to select from. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: the required floor gains a main-push (or scheduled) mode that runs every claim entry rather than the edited-witness selection, and this row's specimen -- plus any red like it -- goes loud on main at the moment it is introduced, before it can be inherited by an unrelated change.",
  ],
  evidence: [],
}
